### Design Studio and Present

Use the repo skills for the complete, current workflows:

- `design-studio` — find, create, pull down, watch, and append design revisions.
- `present` — create or update HTML artifacts and activate them in `/present`.

The normal commands are `graph ui-design "Title" <dir>` for Design Studio and
the same command with `--present` for a new Present artifact. Always search by
exact title first; update an existing stable `design_id` instead of creating a
duplicate. Use `--force` only when a same-named new artifact is intentional.

**Reading a session by tmux name.** `graph read`, `graph context`, and `graph tail` accept either a source-id prefix or the tmux name shown by `graph sessions --status` (e.g. `auto-0506-001257`, `host-0506-095207`). Names containing non-hex characters are auto-resolved through the dashboard DB; pass them directly, no UUID lookup needed.

**Search heuristic.** Lead with the single highest-signal term. Multi-term queries and `--or` widen the candidate set and tend to score the obvious hit *down*, not up. If a multi-term AND query has no hits, the interactive CLI automatically shows clearly labelled any-term fallback results; quoted phrases and `--json` stay strict. If the row you want is buried, scope before widening: `--type session` / `--type note` / `--only-org` / `--tag` all compose. Output is compact by default (one excerpt per source); use `--verbose` only when you need every matching excerpt.

**Reading notes — comments and the trailer.** `graph read <note>` shows open (non-integrated) comments by default; `--all-comments` adds the ones already rolled into the body — only needed for synthesis passes / audits. Every read ends with a trailer like `── 14,328 chars · 287 lines · 19 comments (14 open, 5 integrated) ──`. If you don't see it, you didn't read to the end. If the comment count there exceeds what you rendered, your `--max-chars` or shell pipe (`head`, `tail`) hid feedback — re-read without the cap before drawing conclusions.

**Sharing files with the operator (`graph share`)**

Use `graph share <file> [--alt ...] [--caption ...]` to drop an image (or
any file) into the session viewer as an inline tile. One tool call →
one tile, rendered at the current turn. The operator clicks for fullscreen.

- **One share per Bash tool_result.** The harness up-converts a single JSON
  object whose `type` is `viewer_attachment`; chaining shares (`graph
  share a && graph share b`) in one Bash call concatenates two JSON
  objects and *neither* renders. Use one Bash invocation per share.
- **Don't print anything else in the same Bash call** — extra stdout
  breaks the parse.
- **No `--session` flag, no need.** The session is stamped from the
  trusted JSONL stream, not anything the agent prints.

Canonical how-to with examples + security model: `graph read 3570406f-29a`.

**Dispatch workflow:**
1. `graph dispatch approve <bead-id>` — release bead for dispatch
2. `graph wait <bead-id>` — block until dispatched bead completes
3. `graph dispatch status` — check overall queue at any time

